  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13838",
      "body": "User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d This is approved, but wanted to flag the following: \n\n- If a related colour is added to a product but that related colour has not yet been enabled due to stock, then it shouldn’t appear as a swatch on the PDP until it is enabled. \n- When you are in the expanded Image Gallery view on the PDP there are swatches shown at the top of the gallery. The intended behaviour here is that the product images would change upon rollover of the swatch so the user can see the product quickly in different colours (not a full page load, they stay in the image gallery pop up).",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Dani Rivett",
        "name": "Dani Rivett",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/42d3d7910c25b8f4ba9e46aabfc6c149?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDR-3.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-13T12:31:07.716+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-13T12:31:07.716+1000"
    }
  ],
  "issuelinks": [
    {
      "id": "10588",
      "type": {
        "id": "10003",
        "name": "Relates",
        "inward": "relates to",
        "outward": "relates to",
        "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issueLinkType/10003"
      },
      "outward_issue": {
        "id": "18129",
        "key": "SFCC-91",
        "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18129",
        "fields": {
          "summary": "PDP UI — Colour Swatches & Variation Selection",
          "status": {
            "name": "Ready for Development",
            "category": "To Do",
            "color": "blue-gray"
          },
          "priority": {
            "name": "High"
          },
          "issuetype": {
            "name": "Story"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given a site merchandiser is editing a master product in Business Manager, when they navigate to the product's attributes, then a Related Colours attribute is available.\n2. Given the Related Colours attribute is visible, when the merchandiser enters one or more master product style codes, then the values are saved against that product.\n3. Given the field is populated, when the values are saved, then the order of style codes in the list determines the display order of colour swatches on the PDP.\n4. Given a style code entered in the field does not exist in the catalogue, when the attribute is saved, then no validation error is thrown at save time (the invalid entry is handled at render time).\n\n----\n\nFrom the front-end we still need to test this Acceptance Criteria then, copied from [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-91|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-91|smart-link] :\n\nValid Related Product ID:\nGiven a shopper clicks a colour swatch, when the selection is registered, then the URL updates to reflect the selected colour with a new style code and a full page reload.\n\nInvalid Related Product ID:\nGiven a shopper is on the PDP, when the related colour product IDs are fetched and it's not a valid product ID, then the swatch simply does not render on the PDP."
  },
  "customfield_10016": {
    "value": null
  },
  "customfield_10020": {
    "value": null
  }
}"}

