    "PRD-064",
    "PRD-065",
    "Squad-A",
    "pdp/hero"
  ],
  "updated": "2026-08-13T12:57:57.775+1000",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "Layout — Desktop\n\n1. Given the component is rendered at desktop breakpoint, when the page loads, then the image gallery renders on the left and pdp/product-content renders on the right, with spacing and proportions as defined in the design system.\n2. Given the desktop gallery renders, when the page loads, then it displays carousel items in sequence: single full-width images, and a 4-up 2x2 grid with a View Gallery button overlay on the bottom-right image.\n3. Given the desktop carousel includes a video item, when the component renders, then video control icons (mute and play/pause) are visible in the bottom-right of that carousel item.\n\nLayout — Mobile\n\n4. Given the component is rendered at mobile breakpoint, when the page loads, then the image gallery renders full-width at the top and pdp/product-content renders below it in a stacked column layout with padding as defined in the design system.\n5. Given the component is rendered at mobile breakpoint, when the page loads, then a dot-indicator carousel bar is visible at the bottom-left of the carousel, showing the current position across available images.\n\nshowGalleryButton prop\n\n6. Given showGalleryButton is set to true, when the component renders, then the View Gallery button overlay is visible on the image gallery.\n7. Given showGalleryButton is set to false, when the component renders, then no View Gallery button overlay is shown.\n\nChild component composition\n8. The component does not replicate or override the interaction logic of any child component — size validation, add-to-bag API calls, drawer open/close, and colour swatch selection are all owned by their respective child component stories.\n\nResponsiveness\n\n9. Given the component is rendered, when the viewport transitions between mobile and desktop breakpoints, then the layout switches between stacked and side-by-side configurations with no layout breakage.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)\n\n10. Given a keyboard user navigates through the pdp/hero, when focus moves through the component, then focus order follows the visual reading order: gallery first on desktop (left), product content second (right); stacked top-to-bottom on mobile.\n11. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA as the minimum accessibility standard; child component accessibility is covered in their respective stories."
  },
  "customfield_10016": {
    "value": null
  },
  "customfield_10020": {
    "value": null
  }
}"}

