{"result":"{
  "id": "19170",
  "key": "SFCC-731",
  "summary": "pdp/carousel",
  "description": "As a Developer, I want a reusable pdp/carousel React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can be consumed by pdp/hero to render the product image and video gallery on the PDP.\nThe component renders a sequence of media items (photo and video) in a stacked layout on desktop and a swipeable carousel on mobile. The desktop layout adapts based on total media count. Video is treated as a standard media item and slots into the layout based on its position in the product's media array. The component renders a View Gallery button as a trigger only — the gallery overlay is a separate component and out of scope for this story.\nAcceptance Criteria:\nDesktop layout — media count thresholds\n1. 3 media items → 3 full-width stacked  View Gallery button\n1. 4 media items → 2 full-width  2-up grid  View Gallery button\n1. 5 media items → 2 full-width  2-up grid  View Gallery 1 button\n1. 6 media items → 2 full-width  4-up grid  View Gallery button\n1. 7 media items → 2 full-width  4-up grid  View Gallery X button (X = total minus 6)\n1. Video items slot into the layout based on their position in the media array — they are not treated differently to photo items for layout purposes.\nshowGalleryButton prop\n1. Given showGalleryButton is false, then no View Gallery button renders regardless of media count.\n1. Given showGalleryButton is true, then the View Gallery button renders per the layout thresholds above and is visible and tappable — overlay behaviour is out of scope for this story.\nMobile\n1. Given the component renders on mobile, then all media items display in a swipeable single-image carousel with a dot indicator bar regardless of media count.\n1. Given a shopper swipes, then the active dot indicator updates to reflect the current position.\n1. Given showGalleryButton is true on mobile, then the View Gallery button is visible and tappable.\nEmpty & error states\n1. Given no media items exist for the product, then the component does not render and no broken layout is shown.\n1. Given an image fails to load, then the surrounding layout is maintained without a broken image rendering — fallback behaviour TBD, see open items.\nAccessibility\n1. The carousel is fully keyboard navigable and meets WCAG 2.1 AA.\nOpen Items:\n@Kiera — please confirm media count threshold logic is correct per design specs shared.\n@Kiera — please confirm fallback behaviour when an image fails to load (blank space, grey box, or branded fallback image).",
