{"result":"{
  "id": "19188",
  "key": "SFCC-739",
  "summary": "pdp/gallery",
  "description": "As a Developer, I want a reusable pdp/gallery React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can be triggered from pdp/carousel to render a full-screen product image gallery overlay on the PDP.\n\nThe component renders a full-screen overlay containing a sticky pdp/gallery-header and a scrollable vertical stack of pdp/carousel/item instances. It is triggered by the View Gallery button in pdp/carousel and manages its own open/close state. It does not own the carousel or product content — it receives the product media array as a prop and renders it within the gallery layout.\n\nOpen items:\n\n@Kiera — the gallery overlay and pdp/gallery-header are not yet componentized in the Design System Figma. The design exists in the Designs file (QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs, node 3093-81721). Please extract these into named components in the design system before this story is picked up by a developer.\n\n@Kiera — please confirm AC6: does clicking a model avatar thumbnail scroll to a specific image, or filter the gallery to show only that model's images?",
