  "updated": "2026-08-14T11:20:48.621+1000",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "Overlay shell\n\n1. Given the View Gallery button is clicked in pdp/carousel, then the gallery opens full-screen, taking over the entire viewport.\n2. Given the gallery is open, then clicking the close icon dismisses the overlay and returns the shopper to their previous scroll position on the PDP.\n\npdp/gallery-header — Desktop\n\n3. Given the gallery is open on desktop, then the gallery header is sticky at the top of the overlay and remains visible as the shopper scrolls through images.\n4. Given the gallery header renders on desktop, then it displays: product name, active colour name, close icon, and model avatar thumbnails.\n5. Given the product has multiple colour variants, then the header includes a colour selector in addition to the active colour name.\n6. Given a shopper clicks a model avatar thumbnail in the header, then the gallery scrolls to the corresponding image set for that model.\n7. Given the close icon is clicked, then the gallery closes and focus returns to the View Gallery button that opened it.\n\npdp/gallery-header — Mobile\n\n8. Given the gallery is open on mobile, then the gallery header is sticky at the top of the overlay and remains visible as the shopper scrolls.\n9. Given the gallery header renders on mobile, then it displays: product name, close icon, and colour selector. Model avatar thumbnails are not shown on mobile.\n\nImage content\n\n10. Given the gallery is open, then the full media array renders as a vertically scrollable stack of pdp/carousel/item instances.\n11. Given the gallery renders, then images are served in an optimised format at the appropriate resolution per breakpoint (PRD-063).\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n12. Given no media items are provided, then the gallery does not open and no broken layout is shown.\n13. Given an image fails to load within the gallery, then the image slot maintains its dimensions without breaking the layout.\n\nAccessibility\n\n14. Given the gallery opens, then focus moves into the overlay and is trapped within it until closed.\n15. Given the gallery closes, then focus returns to the View Gallery button that triggered it.\n16. The overlay has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n17. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA."
  },
  "customfield_10016": {
    "value": null
  },
  "customfield_10020": {
    "value": null
  }
}"}

