{"result":"{
  "id": "19189",
  "key": "SFCC-740",
  "summary": "pdp/find-in-boutique",
  "description": "As a Developer, I want a reusable pdp/find-in-boutique React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it renders as a slide-in panel from the right on the PDP when the Find in Boutique link is clicked.\n\nThe panel displays a product summary, a size selector, and a location-aware list of boutiques showing stock availability for the selected product and size. It does not own the Find in Boutique trigger — that is handled by pdp/product-content. The Explore Boutique expanded state is out of scope for this story. Cross-component interactions (size change updating boutique list, location detection) are covered in the PDP functional epic.\n\nOpen items:\n\n@Kiera — this component is not yet componentized in the Design System Figma. The design exists in the PDP drawers section (node 40001369-36929). Please extract into a named component before dev picks this up.\n\n@Kiera — please confirm whether the product summary card at the top of this panel is a shared component (e.g. a horizontal product card variant) and what the canonical component name should be. Note there is already a vertical product card component (node 40000730-13634) so naming should distinguish between the two.",
  "status": {
    "name": "To Do",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "High"
  },
  "parent": {
    "id": "17828",
    "key": "SFCC-2",
    "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/17828",
    "fields": {
      "summary": "PWA Kit Components",
      "status": {
        "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10411",
        "description": "",
        "iconUrl": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/",
        "name": "To Do",
        "id": "10411",
        "statusCategory": {
          "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/2",
          "id": 2,
          "key": "new",
          "colorName": "blue-gray",
          "name": "To Do"
        }
      },
      "priority": {
        "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/1",
        "iconUrl": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/highest_new.svg",
        "name": "Highest",
        "id": "1"
      },
      "issuetype": {
        "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issuetype/10246",
        "id": "10246",
        "description": "Epics track collections of related bugs, stories, and tasks.",
        "iconUrl": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10307?size=medium",
        "name": "Epic",
        "subtask": false,
        "avatarId": 10307,
        "entityId": "e102bd1e-0f8b-4d64-a404-c3d025abab07",
        "hierarchyLevel": 1
      }
    }
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Custom",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "updated": "2026-08-14T11:40:51.978+1000",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "Panel shell\n\n1. Given the Find in Boutique link is clicked, then the panel slides in from the right as defined in the design system.\n2. Given the panel is open, then a close icon is visible in the header and closes the panel on click.\n3. Given the panel content exceeds the panel height, then the content scrolls independently without the header scrolling.\n\nProduct summary\n\n4. Given the panel renders, then it displays the product image, product name, colour, and price at the top of the panel.\n\nSize selector\n\n5. Given the panel renders, then a pdp/size-selector is shown per the spec defined in SFCC-648, including all size states and the Recommended label state where applicable.\n\nStore locator\n\n6. Given the panel renders, then a STORE LOCATORS label displays above the detected city name and a USE LOCATION link.\n\nBoutique list\n\n7. Given the panel renders, then each boutique row displays: boutique name, availability badge, full address, open/closed status with green dot indicator, distance, Directions link, and an Explore Boutique drawer trigger.\n8. Given the component receives an availability status of Available, then the badge renders with that label and a warm background as defined in the design system.\n9. Given the component receives an availability status of Low stock, then the badge renders with that label and a warm background as defined in the design system.\n10. Given the component receives an availability status of Unavailable, then the badge renders with that label and a grey background.\n11. The availability status passed to each boutique row is determined by the inventory integration — that logic is covered in the PDP functional epic.\n12. Given a shopper clicks the Directions link, then it opens directions to that boutique in the device's default maps application.\n13. Given a shopper clicks the Explore Boutique trigger, then it expands to show further boutique detail — the expanded state content is out of scope for this story.\n14. Given no boutiques are found for the selected location and size, then an appropriate empty state message is displayed.\n\nAccessibility\n\n15. Given the panel opens, then focus moves into the panel and is trapped within it until closed.\n16. Given the panel closes, then focus returns to the Find in Boutique link that triggered it.\n17. The panel has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n18. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA."
  },
  "customfield_10016": {
    "value": null
  },
  "customfield_10020": {
    "value": null
  }
}"}

