    "value": "Panel shell\n\n1. Given the Find in Boutique link is clicked, then the panel slides in from the right as defined in the design system.\n2. Given the panel is open, then a close icon is visible in the header and closes the panel on click.\n3. Given the panel content exceeds the panel height, then the content scrolls independently without the header scrolling.\n\nProduct summary\n\n4. Given the panel renders, then it displays the product image, product name, colour, and price at the top of the panel.\n\nSize selector\n\n5. Given the panel renders, then a pdp/size-selector is shown per the spec defined in SFCC-648, including all size states and the Recommended label state where applicable.\n\nStore locator\n\n6. Given the panel renders, then a STORE LOCATORS label displays above the detected city name and a USE LOCATION link.\n\nBoutique list\n\n7. Given the panel renders, then each boutique row displays: boutique name, availability badge, full address, open/closed status with green dot indicator, distance, Directions link, and an Explore Boutique drawer trigger.\n8. Given the component receives an availability status of Available, then the badge renders with that label and a warm background as defined in the design system.\n9. Given the component receives an availability status of Low stock, then the badge renders with that label and a warm background as defined in the design system.\n10. Given the component receives an availability status of Unavailable, then the badge renders with that label and a grey background.\n11. The availability status passed to each boutique row is determined by the inventory integration — that logic is covered in the PDP functional epic.\n12. Given a shopper clicks the Directions link, then it opens directions to that boutique in the device's default maps application.\n13. Given a shopper clicks the Explore Boutique trigger, then it expands to show further boutique detail — the expanded state content is out of scope for this story.\n14. Given no boutiques are found for the selected location and size, then an appropriate empty state message is displayed.\n\nAccessibility\n\n15. Given the panel opens, then focus moves into the panel and is trapped within it until closed.\n16. Given the panel closes, then focus returns to the Find in Boutique link that triggered it.\n17. The panel has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n18. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA."
