  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "Panel shell\n\n1. Given the notify me trigger is fired, then the panel slides in from the right as defined in the design system.\n2. Given the panel is open, then a close icon is visible and closes the panel on click.\n3. Given the panel content exceeds the panel height, then the content scrolls independently without the header scrolling.\n\nProduct summary\n\n4. Given the panel renders, then it displays the product image, product name, colour, size, and price.\n\nForm\n\n5. Given the panel renders, then First name, Last name, and Email input fields render using the Textfield atom per the design system spec, including all states: default, hover, focused, filled, disabled, and error.\n\nNewsletter opt-in\n\n6. Given the panel renders, then a Checkbox atom and opt-in label are visible below the form fields.\n\nLegal\n\n7. Given the panel renders, then the privacy policy consent copy is visible with a tappable Privacy Policy link.\n\nSubmit CTA\n\n8. Given the panel renders, then a NOTIFY ME button is visible — submission behaviour is covered in the PDP functional epic.\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n9. Given the panel fails to load, then no broken layout is shown.\n\nAccessibility\n\n10. Given the panel opens, then focus moves into the panel and is trapped within it until closed.\n11. Given the panel closes, then focus returns to the trigger element that opened it.\n12. The panel has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n13. Given a field-level error is shown, then it is announced via an ARIA live region.\n14. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA."
